      "additions": 78,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc67vLcq",
      "title": "holocene: also require non-zero elasticity in extraData",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 872,
      "body": "**Description**\r\n\r\nExtends the Holocene spec to also require the header `extraData`-embedded elasticity to be non-zero.\r\n\r\nThis is safe to do retroactively because during payload execution, the EIP1559params contained in the payload attributes are either both zero or both non-zero, which itself is guaranteed by how derivation sets those parameters: they are both 0 if nothing has been set yet at the `SystemConfig` contract or both non-zero, which is enforced by [`setEIP1559Params`](https://specs.optimism.io/protocol/holocene/system-config.html#seteip1559params). And if there ever had been a malicious unsafe block with a zero elasticity, it would have [caused a division by zero panic](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/op-geth/blob/6cbfcd5161083bcd4052edc3022d9f99c6fe40e0/consensus/misc/eip1559/eip1559.go#L93).\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-06T14:58:50Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-01-06T20:46:06Z",
      "additions": 3,
      "deletions": 3
    }
  ],
